cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite it as below, and cite the data (WoSIS, WorldClim) and the methods
  it builds on (see README.md, Citation).
title: >-
  Soil relation parameter learning: predicting sparse soil chemistry through the bounded parameters of
  pedological relations (a preliminary pilot)
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Westland
    given-names: Daan
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-09-30
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/DaanWestland/soil-relation-parameter-learning
url: https://github.com/DaanWestland/soil-relation-parameter-learning
abstract: >-
  A preliminary pilot on public data (not peer-reviewed). Sparse soil chemistry (total N, CEC7) is
  predicted through the bounded parameters of pedological relations (C:N ratio, clay activity) pushed
  through the relations with joint draws of abundant properties (clay, organic carbon, pH), and compared
  with free and chained predictions for four learners (quantile regression forest, TabM, TabICLv2 in
  context and fine-tuned) under spatial block cross-validation with controlled label thinning, on WoSIS
  profiles of the conterminous USA (0-30 cm).
keywords:
  - digital soil mapping
  - pedometrics
  - pedotransfer functions
  - parameter learning
  - hybrid machine learning
  - knowledge-guided machine learning
  - probabilistic prediction
  - CRPS
  - spatial cross-validation
  - tabular foundation models
  - quantile regression forest
  - WoSIS
  - cation exchange capacity
  - total nitrogen
